 ],
 "literal": "Dense darkness to disperse, having flashed, coolly / falling drops, sweet, having scattered, in turn / like a drum struck by a drumstick, having roared, thundering repeatedly / rain now, may you live! To obtain, we / the work to be done having finished, with a proud mind / with her, having united, the blue water-lily's / short-stemmed fresh flower smelling sweet / fragrant soft hair, on the soft bed/embrace we are.",
 "translation": "O rain, may you live long! Flash so that the deep darkness is dispersed, scatter sweet falling drops, and roar in turn like a drum beaten with a drumstick, thundering repeatedly as you pour down now! For we, having finished our duty with a proud heart, have united with her, and are now resting in the soft embrace of her fragrant, soft hair that smells of fresh, short-stemmed blue water-lilies.",
 "modern": "அடர்ந்த இருள் விலகும்படி மின்னல் மின்னி, குளிர்ச்சியாக இனிய மழைத்துளிகளைத் தூவி, முறைப்படி குறுந்தடியால் அடிக்கப்படும் முரசு போல முழங்கி, மீண்டும் மீண்டும் இடித்து இப்போது மழை பொழிவாயாக! நீ வாழ்க! கடமையை முடித்த பெருமித உணர்வோடு நாம் இவளுடன் கூடி, குவளையின் குட்டையான தண்டையுடைய புதிய மலரின் மணம் வீசும் நறிய மென்மையான கூந்தலாகிய மெல்லிய அணையில் துயில்கின்றோம்.",
 "explanation": "The hero is speaking to the rain upon his return to his beloved. He has successfully completed his mission and returned to his wife in the Mullai (forest/pastoral) region just as the rainy season begins. He blesses the rain and urges it to pour down generously, now that he is safely back home and reunited with his wife. He describes the thunderous, rhythmic sound of the rain like a beaten drum, and contrasts the wild storm outside with the peaceful, fragrant intimacy of his wife's embrace inside. The Mullai landscape is characterized by the rainy season, which is the time of the hero's promised return. The key words are 'செய்வினை முடித்த' (having finished the task), 'மேவினமாகி' (having united), and 'நறுமென் கூந்தல்' (fragrant soft hair).",
